  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14257592/assets/e90471633ae015ce56a6493d19b4835e38cb3df8d71b989bfe7b8281eaaec286.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(Bx)+3,$ where $B$ is a constant. What is the value of $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}-0=\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{csc}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\pi }{2}=\\frac{2\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is:\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{4}{5}x)+3\n$$",
